        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "A 3.3 V LDO, fed from the 5 V rail, produces 3V3 for “MCUs and Sensors”."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU receives power on its VDD pins, so the flight-control and navigation processors cannot operate. The distinct rail names also leave the intended MCU rail disconnected from the LDO output.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["FCC2", "UART3_FCC2", "C57"],
      "pins": ["FCC2.48", "FCC2.73", "UART3_FCC2.3", "UART3_FCC2.4", "C57.1"],
      "nets": ["NET0020", "NET0034", "unconnected-(C57-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "Both H753 VCAP pins are routed to pins 3 and 4 of the UART3_FCC2 connector, respectively. The 2u2 capacitor C57 is unconnected rather than providing VCAP decoupling.",
      "expected": "VCAP pins are internal-core-regulator outputs and should have the required local capacitors to ground, not be exposed on a UART connector.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"19\") (name \"NET0020\") ... (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"3\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"30\") (name \"NET0034\") ... (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"4\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"166\") (name \"unconnected-(C57-Pad1)\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU core supply outputs are exposed through the UART connector and lack their required decoupling, risking processor malfunction or damage if the connector is used.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["HSE2", "FCC2"],
      "pins": ["HSE2.1", "HSE2.3", "FCC2.5", "FCC2.37"],
      "nets": ["NET0052", "Net-(C96-Pad1)", "Net-(FCC2-PH0)", "VREF+_FCC"],
      "observed": "The FCC HSE2 crystal connects to FCC2.5 (PE6) and FCC2.37 (PE7), while the MCU oscillator pins PH0 and PH1 are on other nets.",
      "expected": "The specified FCC high-speed external crystal should connect to the MCU's HSE oscillator input and output pins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"41\") (name \"NET0052\") ... (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\")) (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"116\") (name \"Net-(C96-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\")) (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"3\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The FCC external crystal cannot clock the MCU through its HSE pins, potentially preventing the intended clock configuration and operation.",
      "confidence": 0.94
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: both MCUs have unconnected VDD pins, the FCC VCAP outputs are routed to a UART connector instead of being decoupled, and the FCC crystal is connected to GPIO pins rather than its oscillator pins."
}

